SUMMARY:Thompson Creek from Mt Pisgah Overlook - 7.5 Mi\, 2400 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nI updated the hike start location 
 as the Pisgah Inn parking lot will be closed. This is my second attempt at
  scheduling this hike. This is a down-then-up\, out-and-back hike making i
 t harder in my opinion. There are some steep and rocky sections so please 
 be prepared for a harder hike and realize up is the only way back. We will
  keep a moderate pace but take breaks for water and to look at the views. 
 I think we will see some nice fall colors.\n\nApproximate hike except star
 ting by Buck Springs Lodge\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/trail/us/north-carol
 ina/thompson-ridge-trail\n\n**CARPOOL**\nLet's meet at the French Broad Ov
 erlook at 9:00. If you want to go directly to the trailhead\, please let m
 e know and use the directions in the link below. We will start hiking in t
 he Mt Pisgah Overlook parking lot by the Buck Springs Lodge/MST trailhead 
 at 9:30 am.\n\nFrench Broad Overlook Location\nhttps://maps.app.goo.gl/2zZ
 s7UcpGFHX9eLw9\n\n**WEATHER**\nThe weather currently might be okay for Mon
 day but I'll watch the weather and post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM 
 if there is a chance of severe weather or lightning during this time perio
 d..\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through MeetUp until 8:00 AM the
  day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to text or call m
 e up to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Ashev
 ille Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to
  and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own safe
 ty and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditionin
 g\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and prop
 erty. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure yo
 ur safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full responsibility
  for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
