SUMMARY:Graybeard Falls -- 6 mi\, 1\,200 ft. gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**PLEASE READ ENTIRE DESCRIPTION B
 ELOW**\n\n**Sign-up opens Sunday\, Nov. 1st at 8 PM**\n\nThe Mt. Graybeard
  Trail is a favorite of many\, myself included. We’ll do an out-and-back
 \, around 3 miles up and the same coming back. There's a clearing by Grayb
 eard Falls where we'll take a short break before heading down.\n\nBecause 
 of a sustained uphill segment and lots of heads-down walking over roots & 
 rocks\, this hike earns a solid 5.0 difficulty level on a 10-point scale. 
 If you ever use hiking poles\, they'd be useful here. Parts of the uphill 
 are definitely not in the "easy" category\, so if you're a less experience
 d hiker and unsure whether you're okay with 1\,000'+ in elevation gain\, i
 t's best to sit this one out rather than risk holding back the group. We'l
 l move at a fairly good pace\, averaging around 2.2 mph.\n\nThere are thre
 e stream crossings. One via a relatively new bridge\, and the other two re
 quire some rock-hopping. The trail can be muddy in parts\, too\, so wear g
 ood hiking shoes.\n\n***Dog Policy:*** Dogs are welcome but must be leashe
 d.\n\n***Guest Policy:*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, they'll need to
  join the Asheville Hiking Group and sign up for the hike on their own. Al
 ternatively\, if you've made it onto the "Going" list\, contact me in adva
 nce to check whether it's okay to bring a "+1". Depending on timing and de
 mand\, we may be able to add your guest.\n\n**MEET-UP TIME & PLACE**\n\nPa
 rking at the trailhead is very tight\, so carpooling is a must. We'll meet
  at the **Black Mountain Ingles at 550 Route NC-9\, which is near Exit 64 
 off I-40.** We'll **leave promptly at 8:45\,** so please arrive early for 
 check-in and organizing rides.\n\nWe’ll gather at the **north end** of t
 he Ingles parking lot toward McDonald's (but not in the McD's lot)\, which
  is toward the right when you enter the Ingles lot. Look for my car\, a si
 lver Hyundai sedan.\n\nOn Google Maps: **[https://bit.ly/3TLR4yG](https://
 bit.ly/3TLR4yG)**\n\n**COURTESY TO WAIT-LISTERS**\nOnly sign up if you def
 initely plan to come. If you must cancel\, please change your status to "N
 ot Going" as soon as possible so wait-listers can have sufficient notice. 
 And please please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n\nIf you're on the waiting l
 ist\, keep checking through the evening before the hike. We often get last
 -minute dropouts. Also\, if you know at some point that you won't be able 
 to attend even if someone drops out\, please remove yourself from the wait
 ing list.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch the weather and post a cancellation m
 essage by 7:30 AM if the forecast is >50% chance of precipitation.\n\n**QU
 ESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through MeetUp until 8:30 AM the day of. Ce
 ll reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to text me up to the start o
 f the hike: (803) 767-3094.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group e
 vent involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetu
 p site. Participants are responsible for their own safety and affirm that 
 they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and
  supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your 
 hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor elimi
 nate all risks. Participants assume full responsibility for any injuries\,
  damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/317203564
 /
